{"qid":"Q754","names":["Republic of Trinidad and Tobago"],"title":"Republic of Trinidad and Tobago","endonym":{"native":"Republic of Trinidad and Tobago","lang":"en"},"capsule":"Trinidad and Tobago is a twin-island republic at the southern extremity of the Caribbean chain, achieving independence from the United Kingdom on 31 August 1962 under Prime Minister Eric Williams of the People's National Movement and becoming a republic within the Commonwealth on 1 August 1976. The country's substantial petroleum and natural gas reserves, exploited commercially from the early twentieth century, have made it among the most industrialised economies in the anglophone Caribbean, with the Point Lisas complex producing ammonia, methanol, and LNG for export. Trinidad is also the birthplace of steelpan music and calypso, and hosts one of the largest carnivals in the Western Hemisphere.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. As a modern sovereign state with internationally recognised borders comprising the two main islands and smaller dependencies, the territorial extent of Trinidad and Tobago is fully and precisely defined.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Trinidad and Tobago","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_and_Tobago"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Eric Williams (politician)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Williams_(politician)"},{"label":"Wikipedia: History of Trinidad and Tobago","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Trinidad_and_Tobago"}],"britannica":"place/Trinidad-and-Tobago","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Trinidad and Tobago","rulers":[{"qid":"Q1338879","name":"Eric Williams","sta